# Velocity Integration Simulator

An interactive Python educational tool for calculating,
visualizing, and solving definite integrals applied to
velocity and displacement problems.

## 🎯 Objective

This project was developed as an educational resource to help
students understand the relationship between velocity,
displacement, and definite integrals through Python.

The program allows users to define an initial and final time,
calculate the distance traveled through numerical integration,
and visualize the corresponding area under the velocity-time
curve.

## 🧮 Integral Visualization and Calculation

The project demonstrates how Python can be used to both
**solve and visualize definite integrals**.

A velocity function is defined as:

v(t) = 2t² + 3t + 2

The distance traveled between two time instants is obtained
by integrating the velocity function over the selected
interval.

The result is then represented graphically as the area under
the velocity-time curve.

## 📊 Visualization

The program generates a velocity-versus-time graph and
highlights the integration interval.

This provides a visual interpretation of the definite
integral and its physical meaning as accumulated distance.

## 🛠️ Technologies

- Python
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- SciPy
- Numerical Integration

## 🔬 Computational Methods

The project uses `scipy.integrate.quad` to perform numerical
integration of the velocity function.

This demonstrates how computational tools can be used to solve
definite integrals and connect numerical results with their
graphical representation.

